"installs":198,"stars":1,"versions":2},"createdAt":1771876982888,"updatedAt":1779077248498,"latestVersion":{"version":"2.0.0","createdAt":1772243550692,"changelog":"Self-Evolution v2.0.0 – Major research-backed upgrade\n\n- Integrated AI safety frameworks from MIRI, DeepMind, and OpenAI for safe self-modification, corrigibility, and rollback capability.\n- Embedded meta-learning algorithms (MAML, Reptile, Meta-SGD) enabling much faster, research-based skill acquisition and rapid adaptation.\n- Added intrinsic motivation and curiosity-driven exploration based on leading reinforcement learning principles.\n- Enhanced continual learning using techniques to prevent catastrophic forgetting and ensure knowledge retention.\n- Updated documentation for evidence-based capabilities, clearer safety guardrails, and research sources.\n- Added PLANNED.md to document future evolution plans and roadmap.","license":null},"metadata":{"setup":[],"os":["darwin","linux","win32"],"systems":null}},{"ownerHandle":"al-one","slug":"taobao","displayName":"🛍️ 淘宝/京东/拼多多比价技能","summary":"商品价格全网对比技能，获取商品在淘宝(Taobao)、天猫(TMall)、京东(JD.com)、拼多多(PinDuoDuo)、抖音(Douyin)、快手(KaiShou)的最优价格、优惠券，当用户想购物或者获取优惠信息时使用。Get the best price, coupons for goods on Chi...","description":null,"topics":["购物"],"tags":{"latest":"1.0.3"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":6938,"installs":196,"stars":16,"versions":4},"createdAt":1771837657980,"updatedAt":1778491617178,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.3","createdAt":1773651713924,"changelog":"- Expanded supported shopping platforms in source options (added 全部, 苏宁, 唯品会, 考拉, 1688).\n- Updated default search examples to use 全部平台 (source=0).\n- Refined and clarified skill description for broader coverage.\n- No code or file changes detected; documentation updates only.","license":"MIT-0"},"metadata":{"setup":[],"os":null,"systems":null}},{"ownerHandle":"wesley138cn","slug":"feishu-sheets-skill","displayName":"Feishu Sheets Skill","summary":"Feishu online spreadsheet (Sheets) operations including create, read, write, append data, manage worksheets. Use when user mentions Feishu Sheets, online spr...","description":null,"topics":["Feishu","Spreadsheet"],"tags":{"latest":"1.0.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":6933,"installs":235,"stars":7,"versions":1},"createdAt":1771220240776,"updatedAt":1778491552996,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1771220240776,"changelog":"Initial release: Feishu online spreadsheet operations including create, read, write, append, insert/delete rows/columns, manage worksheets","license":null},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"ivangdavila","slug":"designer","displayName":"Designer","summary":"Operates as the designer on a job: decides what to make, makes it, defends it in review, and hands over files that can actually be built. Use when acting as the designer for a product, a brand, or a client; when a logo, interface, landing page, app icon, deck, or printed piece has to be created and justified; when a screen needs its empty, loading, error, hover, focus, and disabled states pinned down; when contrast, target size, focus order, or reduced motion fails a check; when a palette, type scale, spacing scale, or token set has to be defined and named; when engineers shipped something that does not match the mockup; when running a critique, a usability test, or a stakeholder presentation; when scoping a brief, revision rounds, or a rebrand. Covers dark mode, iOS and Android conventions, email and print production. Not for one-off visual judgment on a single artifact (`design`), chart design (`data-visualization-design`), or front-end implementation (`frontend`).","description":null,"topics":[],"tags":{"latest":"1.0.2"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":6927,"installs":151,"stars":4,"versions":3},"createdAt":1770672498010,"updatedAt":1785141712726,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.2","createdAt":1785140530444,"changelog":"Clearer disclosure of what is stored and where","license":"MIT-0"},"metadata":{"setup":[],"os":["linux","darwin","win32"],"systems":null}},{"ownerHandle":"artyomx33","slug":"first-principles-decomposer","displayName":"First Principles Decomposer","summary":"Break any problem down to fundamental truths, then rebuild solutions from atoms up. Use when user says \"firstp\", \"first principles\", \"from scratch\", \"what are we assuming\", \"break this down\", \"atomic\", \"fundamental truth\", \"physics thinking\", \"Elon method\", \"bedrock\", \"ground up\", \"core problem\", \"strip away\", or challenges assumptions about how things are done.","description":null,"topics":[],"tags":{"latest":"1.0.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":6923,"installs":238,"stars":17,"versions":1},"createdAt":1769359768223,"updatedAt":1778485852489,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1769359768223,"changelog":"Initial release - Break problems to fundamental truths, rebuild from atoms. By Artem Tolmachev & Claude.","license":null},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"millibus","slug":"smart-model-switching","displayName":"Smart Model Switching","summary":"Auto-route tasks to the cheapest Claude model that works correctly. Three-tier progression: Haiku → Sonnet → Opus. Classify before responding. HAIKU (default): factual Q&A, greetings, reminders, status checks, lookups, simple file ops, heartbeats, casual chat, 1-2 sentence tasks. ESCALATE TO SONNET: code >10 lines, analysis, comparisons, planning, reports, multi-step reasoning, tables, long writing >3 paragraphs, summarization, research synthesis, most user conversations. ESCALATE TO OPUS: architecture decisions, complex debugging, multi-file refactoring, strategic planning, nuanced judgment, deep research, critical production decisions. Rule: If a human needs >30 seconds of focused thinking, escalate. If Sonnet struggles with complexity, go to Opus. Save 50-90% on API costs by starting cheap and escalating only when needed.","description":null,"topics":["Debugging"],"tags":{"latest":"1.0.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":6920,"installs":243,"stars":21,"versions":1},"createdAt":1770213230022,"updatedAt":1778486017068,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770213230022,"changelog":"Initial release - Three-tier Claude routing for cost optimization","license":null},"metadata":{"setup":[],"os":null,"systems":null}},{"ownerHandle":"mrblackerx","slug":"stock","displayName":"股票查询","summary":"查询A股、港股、美股股票的实时行情，包括价格、涨跌幅、开盘价、成交量等详细数据。","description":null,"topics":["Stock","股票"],"tags":{"latest":"1.0.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":6914,"installs":170,"stars":0,"versions":1},"createdAt":1772343297159,"updatedAt":1778491674555,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1772343297159,"changelog":"Initial release of Stock Skill - 股票查询\n\n- Query real-time stock data for A-shares, Hong Kong stocks, and US stocks.\n- Supports automatic market identification for A-shares (Shanghai/Shenzhen).\n- Retrieves information using Sina Finance API.\n- Outputs current price, change percentage and amount, open/high/low price, trading volume/value, and turnover rate.","license":null},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"shaharsha","slug":"google-weather","displayName":"Google Weather","summary":"Google Weather API - accurate, real-time weather data. Get current conditions, temperature, humidity, wind, and forecasts. Powered by Google's Weather API fo...","description":null,"topics":["Weather","Google","Current Conditions","Humidity","Real Time"],"tags":{"api":"1.0.0","climate":"1.0.0","current-conditions":"1.0.0","forecast":"1.0.0","google":"1.0.0","humidity":"1.0.0","latest":"1.3.0","real-time":"1.0.0","temperature":"1.0.0","weather":"1.0.0","wind":"1.0.0"},"stats":{"comments":2,"downloads":6911,"installs":239,"stars":5,"versions":8},"createdAt":1770216081308,"updatedAt":1778486017068,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.3.0","createdAt":1774205682220,"changelog":"**Added unit system selection (metric/imperial) via environment variable**\n\n- Support for `GOOGLE_WEATHER_UNITS` environment variable to choose metric or imperial units.\n- Weather output now displays values (temperature, wind, etc.) in the selected unit system.\n- Documentation updated: details and example outputs for both metric and imperial modes.\n- No code changes required for unit switching—set the environment variable and restart.","license":"MIT-0"},"metadata":{"setup":[{"key":"GOOGLE_API_KEY","required":true}],"os":null,"systems":null}},{"ownerHandle":"hith3sh","slug":"gmail-email","displayName":"Gmail","summary":"Read, search, draft, reply to, and organize Gmail from chat via the Gmail API. Use this skill when users want an inbox copilot — search and fetch messages, read by thread, list labels, create and send drafts, reply to threads, forward messages, manage labels, archive or trash messages, and retrieve attachment content.","description":null,"topics":["Gmail","Email"],"tags":{"latest":"1.0.9"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":6908,"installs":81,"stars":32,"versions":7},"createdAt":1777753778420,"updatedAt":1785326347367,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.9","createdAt":1785317639998,"changelog":"Accuracy pass on permissions and troubleshooting. Corrects the scope description to the real full-mailbox OAuth grant (was 'scoped to the mailbox'), documents that gmail_fetch_emails defaults max_results to 1, adds the Gmail query-operator list, the spam/trash exclusion, and label-ids-vs-names. Rewrites the 403 row to lead with placeholder/example IDs (the most common real cause) instead of scopes, and adds a row for tokens invalidated by a Google password change.","license":"MIT-0"},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"impkind","slug":"hippocampus-memory","displayName":"Hippocampus","summary":"Persistent memory system for AI agents. Automatic encoding, decay, and semantic reinforcement — just like the hippocampus in your brain. Based on Stanford Generative Agents (Park et al., 2023).","description":null,"topics":["Memory System"],"tags":{"latest":"3.8.6"},"stats":{"comments":2,"downloads":6906,"installs":236,"stars":24,"versions":10},"createdAt":1769896469487,"updatedAt":1779076551570,"latestVersion":{"version":"3.8.6","createdAt":1770323640353,"changelog":"- Skill name updated to \"hippocampus-memory\" and title clarified.\n- Description rewritten for clarity and conciseness.\n- Metadata version bumped to 3.8.6.\n- Documentation restructured for easier reading; headings clarified and formatting improved.\n- No changes to scripts, features, or usage—documentation improvements only.","license":null},"metadata":{"setup":[],"os":null,"systems":null}},{"ownerHandle":"javicasper","slug":"reddit-scraper","displayName":"Reddit Scraper","summary":"Read and search Reddit posts via web scraping of old.reddit.com. Use when Clawdbot needs to browse Reddit content - read posts from subreddits, search for topics, monitor specific communities. Read-only access with no posting or comments.","description":null,"topics":["Web Scraping"],"tags":{"latest":"1.0.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":6884,"installs":241,"stars":8,"versions":1},"createdAt":1769552693110,"updatedAt":1778485863829,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1769552693110,"changelog":"Initial release: JSON API, search, short links, flairs","license":null},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"gxcun17","slug":"skywork-ppt","displayName":"Skywork PPT","summary":"Skywork PPT (skywork) - Use when the user wants to work with PowerPoint presentations. Triggers: (1) Generate a new PPT from a topic — 'generate a PPT', 'cre...","description":null,"topics":["PDF"],"tags":{"latest":"1.0.9"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":6883,"installs":208,"stars":33,"versions":10},"createdAt":1773661121344,"updatedAt":1778491948843,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.9","createdAt":1776949188398,"changelog":"**Added support for converting NotebookLM-exported files to editable PPTX.**\n\n- New capability: Convert .pptx or .pdf exported from NotebookLM to fully editable PPTX format (Layer 5).\n- Added script: scripts/run_editable_convert.py to handle the conversion process.\n- Added workflow guide: workflow_convert_editable.md.\n- Updated skill description and workflow to include the new conversion feature.","license":"MIT-0"},"metadata":{"setup":[{"key":"SKYWORK_API_KEY","required":true}],"os":null,"systems":null}},{"ownerHandle":"byungkyu","slug":"chargebee","displayName":"chargebee","summary":"Chargebee API integration with managed OAuth. Install only if you need Chargebee billing administration. Connect with least-privilege access, verify the intended connection ID before each request, and revoke unused connections promptly. This integration can mutate billing data — approve only specific write actions after checking the exact endpoint, account, resource ID, and consequence. For other third party apps, use the api-gateway skill (https://clawhub.ai/byungkyu/api-gateway). Calls run through the `maton` CLI with OAuth login, or over raw HTTP with a Maton API key where the CLI cannot be installed. Every call is authenticated as the user's connection and reaches only what that connection's authorization allows, which the provider enforces on every request; the endpoints documented here are the ones this skill uses, and any other endpoint of this app needs the user to ask for it by name. Default to read and list calls, and confirm every write or new connection with the user. This file also documents the three constructs that turn a Chargebee connection into automation, in the order they are used: the connection (the first step), a hosted function that runs a Chargebee action through the Maton SDK, and a trigger that calls that function on a schedule or on an event. Those sections are the platform's own reference text, shared with the api-gateway skill, with Chargebee examples; they add no Chargebee capability - Chargebee is not an event source, a trigger cannot read Chargebee data, and the files under `references/<source>/triggers.md` are the platform's event catalogues for the sources Maton offers (time, Calendly, GitHub, Gmail, HubSpot, Linear, Notion, Slack, Stripe).","description":null,"topics":["Api Integration"],"tags":{"latest":"1.2.5"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":6880,"installs":217,"stars":3,"versions":15},"createdAt":1770020111858,"updatedAt":1790936528808,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.2.5","createdAt":1790936391458,"changelog":"Simplify the login instructions to the code flow (maton login prints a link; finish with maton login --code <CODE>), drop the API Key subsection, and pin the Maton CLI install to 0.4.0.","license":"MIT-0"},"metadata":{"setup":[],"os":null,"systems":null}},{"ownerHandle":"lstpsche","slug":"gog-calendar","displayName":"Google Calendar (via gogcli)","summary":"Access and manage Google Calendar events with gogcli for cross-calendar agendas, keyword search, and filtered outputs avoiding unwanted calendars like holidays.","description":null,"topics":["Calendar","Json"],"tags":{"agenda":"1.0.0","calendar":"1.0.0","events":"1.0.0","gogcli":"1.0.0","google-calendar":"1.0.0","latest":"1.0.0","productivity":"1.0.0","schedule":"1.0.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":6880,"installs":231,"stars":5,"versions":1},"createdAt":1770157121546,"updatedAt":1778486013286,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770157121546,"changelog":"Initial release of the dedicated gog-calendar skill for cross-calendar agenda and keyword search via gogcli.\n\n- Provides reliable agenda listings (today/week/custom range) by querying all calendars and applying customizable exclusions (e.g., holidays).\n- Supports best-effort keyword search by iterating/aggregating across calendars, with structured output (plain or JSON as appropriate).\n- Optimizes output for token efficiency—defaults to --plain except when structure is required.\n- Post-filters unwanted calendars by name/summary (e.g., holidays), with user or default exclusion rules.\n- Requires explicit user confirmation before any calendar write/modification.","license":null},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"kelevis","slug":"document-summary","displayName":"Document Summary","summary":"Summarizes technical documents into structured markdown.","description":null,"topics":["Document","Summary","Markdown","Technical"],"tags":{"latest":"1.1.1"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":6878,"installs":212,"stars":3,"versions":4},"createdAt":1772615517562,"updatedAt":1778491714733,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.1.1","createdAt":1772618853835,"changelog":"- Added .clawhub/origin.json configuration file.\n- No changes to skill functionality or documentation.","license":null},"metadata":{"setup":[],"os":null,"systems":null}},{"ownerHandle":"robbyczgw-cla","slug":"sports-ticker","displayName":"sports-ticker","summary":"Live sports alerts for Soccer, NFL, NBA, NHL, MLB, F1 and more. Real-time scoring with the free ESPN API. Track any team from any major league worldwide.","description":null,"topics":[],"tags":{"latest":"3.3.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":6873,"installs":227,"stars":2,"versions":29},"createdAt":1768912059920,"updatedAt":1788193163379,"latestVersion":{"version":"3.3.0","createdAt":1788193023955,"changelog":"OpenClaw 2.0 compatibility: corrected frontmatter, automations CLI, and documentation. Verified against a live OpenClaw 2026.8.1 install.","license":"MIT-0"},"metadata":{"setup":[],"os":null,"systems":null}},{"ownerHandle":"galizki","slug":"evoweb-ai","displayName":"EvoWeb.ai Website Builder","summary":"Create a Website in 4 Minutes Designed to Bring Clients from ChatGPT, Gemini & Modern Search","description":null,"topics":["Website"],"tags":{"latest":"1.0.10"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":6869,"installs":235,"stars":11,"versions":11},"createdAt":1769862042613,"updatedAt":1778485878349,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.10","createdAt":1771056125974,"changelog":"- Added workflow for users without an API key: allows starting website creation via a personalized registration link using a brief (max 250 characters) business description.\n- Simplified prompt handling: focus only on the essential business description; no need to specify design, sections, or layout.\n- Updated polling interval for status checks to every 1 minute (was 15–20 seconds).\n- Live and editor URLs updated to new domains in responses.\n- Retry endpoint now also supports sites with \"ready\" status in addition to \"failed\" status.\n- Documentation streamlined with clearer instructions and improved onboarding for new users.","license":null},"metadata":{"setup":[{"key":"EVOWEB_API_KEY","required":true}],"os":null,"systems":null}},{"ownerHandle":"arnarsson","slug":"curl-http","displayName":"Curl Http","summary":"Essential curl commands for HTTP requests, API testing, and file transfers.","description":null,"topics":[],"tags":{"latest":"1.0.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":6868,"installs":241,"stars":6,"versions":1},"createdAt":1769692053458,"updatedAt":1778485868789,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1769692053458,"changelog":"curl-http 1.0.0 – Initial Release\n\n- Provides essential curl command examples for HTTP requests, API testing, and file transfers.\n- Covers usage for GET, POST, PUT, DELETE, and PATCH requests, authentication methods, custom headers, cookies, proxy, and SSL/TLS options.\n- Includes examples for file downloads/uploads, response formatting, range requests, and performance testing.\n- Offers tips for scripting, debugging, and common usage patterns.\n- Lists helpful curl flags and links to official documentation.","license":null},"metadata":{"setup":[],"os":null,"systems":null}},{"ownerHandle":"jau123","slug":"creative-toolkit","displayName":"MeiGen","summary":"Compose MeiGen image/video and five dedicated image tools inside an existing workflow, or opt into creative planning. Preserves caller prompts, parameters, approved count and budget; includes discovery and recoverable task handles.","description":null,"topics":["Video Editing","Prompt","image-generation"],"tags":{"latest":"3.2.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":6862,"installs":147,"stars":7,"versions":44},"createdAt":1770983443866,"updatedAt":1791805780754,"latestVersion":{"version":"3.2.0","createdAt":1791805675254,"changelog":"Guide reference-media imports, strict frame/content roles, live pricing and OAuth-only saved characters; retain search, favorites and legacy compatibility boundaries.","license":"MIT-0"},"metadata":{"setup":[],"os":null,"systems":null}},{"ownerHandle":"vacinc","slug":"simple-backup","displayName":"Simple Backup","summary":"Backup agent brain (workspace) and body (state) to local folder and optionally sync to cloud via rclone.","description":null,"topics":["Backup"],"tags":{"latest":"2.2.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":6853,"installs":238,"stars":4,"versions":9},"createdAt":1768062736818,"updatedAt":1778485729679,"latestVersion":{"version":"2.2.0","createdAt":1769968895366,"changelog":"Added manual override support for custom setups. Priority: config → env → auto-detect. All paths now overridable via skill config.","license":null},"metadata":{"setup":[],"os":null,"systems":null}},{"ownerHandle":"byungkyu","slug":"microsoft-to-do","displayName":"microsoft-to-do","summary":"Microsoft To Do API integration with managed OAuth. Manage task lists, tasks, checklist items, and linked resources. Use this skill when users want to create, read, update, or delete tasks and task lists in Microsoft To Do. For other third party apps, use the api-gateway skill (https://clawhub.ai/byungkyu/api-gateway). Requires network access and valid Maton API key. Calls run through the `maton` CLI with OAuth login, or over raw HTTP with a Maton API key where the CLI cannot be installed. Every call is authenticated as the user's connection and reaches only what that connection's authorization allows, which the provider enforces on every request; the endpoints documented here are the ones this skill uses, and any other endpoint of this app needs the user to ask for it by name. Default to read and list calls, and confirm every write or new connection with the user. This file also documents the three constructs that turn a Microsoft To Do connection into automation, in the order they are used: the connection (the first step), a hosted function that runs a Microsoft To Do action through the Maton SDK, and a trigger that calls that function on a schedule or on an event. Those sections are the platform's own reference text, shared with the api-gateway skill, with Microsoft To Do examples; they add no Microsoft To Do capability - Microsoft To Do is not an event source, a trigger cannot read Microsoft To Do data, and the files under `references/<source>/triggers.md` are the platform's event catalogues for the sources Maton offers (time, Calendly, GitHub, Gmail, HubSpot, Linear, Notion, Slack, Stripe).","description":null,"topics":["Api Integration"],"tags":{"latest":"1.2.5"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":6846,"installs":210,"stars":8,"versions":11},"createdAt":1770496376272,"updatedAt":1790939223454,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.2.5","createdAt":1790939087540,"changelog":"Simplify the login instructions to the code flow (maton login prints a link; finish with maton login --code <CODE>), drop the API Key subsection, and pin the Maton CLI install to 0.4.0.","license":"MIT-0"},"metadata":{"setup":[],"os":null,"systems":null}},{"ownerHandle":"wazionapps","slug":"nexo-brain","displayName":"NEXO Desktop Runtime","summary":"Runtime core for NEXO Desktop. Provides local memory, Deep Sleep, Evolution support-ticket mode, skills, watchdog, and MCP tools for the desktop product.","description":null,"topics":[],"tags":{"latest":"7.38.7"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":6836,"installs":163,"stars":3,"versions":245},"createdAt":1774257674478,"updatedAt":1782628196486,"latestVersion":{"version":"7.38.7","createdAt":1782628196486,"changelog":"Release v7.38.7 - NEXO Desktop runtime core","license":"MIT-0"},"metadata":{"setup":[],"os":["darwin","linux"],"systems":null}},{"ownerHandle":"doonot","slug":"zero-trust","displayName":"Zero Trust","summary":"Security-first behavioral guidelines for cautious agent operation. Use this skill for ALL operations involving external resources, installations, credentials, or actions with external effects. Triggers on - any URL/link interaction, package installations, API key handling, sending emails/messages, social media posts, financial transactions, or any action that could expose data or have irreversible effects.","description":null,"topics":["Financial"],"tags":{"latest":"1.0.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":6833,"installs":234,"stars":13,"versions":1},"createdAt":1770042199717,"updatedAt":1778485994101,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770042199717,"changelog":"**Initial release: Establishes security-first protocols for all high-risk operations.**\n\n- Introduces zero-trust guidelines for agent operations involving external resources, installations, or credentials.\n- Requires explicit human approval for sensitive actions such as sending emails, installing packages, or clicking unknown links.\n- Outlines STOP → THINK → VERIFY → ASK → ACT → LOG flow for all external actions.\n- Defines strict credentials handling: never log or expose, always store securely.\n- Provides clear red flags to identify risky operations and immediate STOP criteria.","license":null},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"byungkyu","slug":"google-contacts","displayName":"google-contacts","summary":"Google Contacts API integration with managed OAuth. Manage contacts, contact groups, and search your address book. Use this skill when users want to create, read, update, or delete contacts, manage contact groups, or search for people in their Google account. For other third party apps, use the api-gateway skill (https://clawhub.ai/byungkyu/api-gateway). Calls run through the `maton` CLI with OAuth login, or over raw HTTP with a Maton API key where the CLI cannot be installed. Every call is authenticated as the user's connection and reaches only what that connection's authorization allows, which the provider enforces on every request; the endpoints documented here are the ones this skill uses, and any other endpoint of this app needs the user to ask for it by name. Default to read and list calls, and confirm every write or new connection with the user. This file also documents the three constructs that turn a Google Contacts connection into automation, in the order they are used: the connection (the first step), a hosted function that runs a Google Contacts action through the Maton SDK, and a trigger that calls that function on a schedule or on an event. Those sections are the platform's own reference text, shared with the api-gateway skill, with Google Contacts examples; they add no Google Contacts capability - Google Contacts is not an event source, a trigger cannot read Google Contacts data, and the files under `references/<source>/triggers.md` are the platform's event catalogues for the sources Maton offers (time, Calendly, GitHub, Gmail, HubSpot, Linear, Notion, Slack, Stripe).","description":null,"topics":["Api Integration"],"tags":{"latest":"1.2.6"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":6832,"installs":233,"stars":5,"versions":13},"createdAt":1770463319244,"updatedAt":1790937736491,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.2.6","createdAt":1790937616494,"changelog":"Simplify the login instructions to the code flow (maton login prints a link; finish with maton login --code <CODE>), drop the API Key subsection, and pin the Maton CLI install to 0.4.0.","license":"MIT-0"},"metadata":{"setup":[],"os":null,"systems":null}},{"ownerHandle":"mvarrieur","slug":"imap-email","displayName":"IMAP Email Reader","summary":"Read and manage email via IMAP (ProtonMail Bridge, Gmail, etc.). Check for new/unread messages, fetch content, search mailboxes, and mark as read/unread. Works with any IMAP server including ProtonMail Bridge.","description":null,"topics":["Email","Gmail"],"tags":{"latest":"1.0.3"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":6831,"installs":232,"stars":1,"versions":4},"createdAt":1769365320036,"updatedAt":1779076473007,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.3","createdAt":1770823426808,"changelog":"Added security metadata (skill.json) declaring credentials and install requirements. Removed redundant README.md.","license":null},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"willykinfoussia","slug":"notion-cli","displayName":"Notion Manager","summary":"Notion CLI for creating and managing pages, databases, and blocks.","description":null,"topics":["Notion"],"tags":{"latest":"0.0.1"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":6815,"installs":232,"stars":8,"versions":1},"createdAt":1770245226102,"updatedAt":1778486022044,"latestVersion":{"version":"0.0.1","createdAt":1770245226102,"changelog":"Version 1.0.0\n\n- Initial release of notion-cli skill.\n- Provides comprehensive CLI documentation for interacting with Notion pages, databases, and blocks.\n- Includes setup instructions, environment requirements, and authentication setup.\n- Features usage examples for searching, retrieving, creating, updating, and querying Notion content.\n- Details property formats and common command patterns for managing Notion data via the CLI.\n- Lists key capabilities such as interactive mode, multiple output formats, and complex filter support.","license":null},"metadata":{"setup":[{"key":"NOTION_TOKEN","required":true}],"os":null,"systems":null}},{"ownerHandle":"arthasking123","slug":"ai-data-analysis","displayName":"AI Data Analysis","summary":"Automates CSV/Excel data cleaning, statistical analysis, trend detection, anomaly identification, visualization, and report generation.","description":null,"topics":["数据处理","Data Analysis"],"tags":{"latest":"1.0.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":6810,"installs":215,"stars":3,"versions":1},"createdAt":1771571081607,"updatedAt":1778991822914,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1771571081607,"changelog":"Initial release","license":null},"metadata":null},{"ownerHand